contentText:
You&#8217;d be surprised by how much 50 Cent was making per episode during his time playing the role Kanan Stark on his hit series Power .

The Queens mogul recently sat down with GQ to talk about his most iconic films and spoke on his friction with writer and showrunner Courtney Kemp Agboh and the show&#8217;s lead Omari Hardwick while also revealing that he took quite the pay cut to play the notorious character. 50 began talking about how his name being attached to the show and his executive producer status made things &#8220;awkward&#8221; for Kemp and Hardwick once the series started to take off in popularity.

